    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "NC-822M\nPAN AMERICAN AIRMAYS SYSTEM",
      "FOTO No. (MIAMI\n137\nBRAZILIAN CLIPPER IN ITS HEYDAY\nPan American World Airways' famous Brazilian\nClipper soars majestically through the air in the\n. mid-thirties, when airmen hailed it as the world's\ngreatest airliner. Retired after a long and\nglorious career on PAA's far-flung Latin American\naerial routes, the one-time queen of the skyways\nhas been shorn of its wings and converted into a\nsix-room Iloating house for a Miami, Fla., family.\n# #\n#\nOABDDG: Blin\nPHOTO BY-\nPAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS SYSTEM\nFOR FURTHER REFERENCE TO THIS PICTURE IDENTIFY BY NUMBER AND ADDRESS PUBLIC RELATIONS, LATIN AMERICAN DIVISION\nFORM E42-68 A (MIME)"
    ],
